# The published list of the occurrence taggings of an entry's program before its lemma rounds (OccurrenceTaggingOption): untagged, the program as the cell gives it; names_and_closures, each lambda chain and each shared part of the program tagged as an occurrence (gezi.frontend.ProgramOccurrences), so that a library whose lemmas type each occurrence on its own (the HM baseline's) has occurrences to start from on a point whose library terms are inlined. Every entry writes one; gezi.contest.entry.Defaults.occurrencesTagged maps it to what the entry does.
# A Scott sum whose constructors are the tuple's fields, in the order of the
# enum's cases; an entry.lambdalattice imports this file and writes a
# constructor, and EntryData reads which alternative it takes by structure
# (gezi.contest.entry.EntryData, THE OPTIONS AS SCOTT CONSTRUCTORS).
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λuntagged names_and_closures. untagged)
λ untagged
. (λtuple. tuple λuntagged names_and_closures. names_and_closures)
λ names_and_closures
. export untagged names_and_closures
